    {
      "id": "waterbird-dynamics-junagadh-wetlands",
      "slug": "waterbird-dynamics-junagadh-wetlands",
      "title": "Waterbird Dynamics: Tracking Hunting Behaviours in Junagadh's Wetlands",
      "category": "Conservation & Fieldwork",
      "author": "Mihir Ranva",
      "published_date": "October 24, 2026",
      "excerpt": "Fieldwork requires patience before the frame. In this study, we break down how analytical tracking systems help map out the migratory movements of local species across the wetlands.",
      "cover_image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/uq0zgy3i/image/upload/q_auto,f_auto,w_1600/lion_pride_13_q5bwgp.jpg",
      "cover_caption": "Figure 1: Rare documentation of hunting sequences captured at Lal Dhori.",
      "reading_time": "4 min read",
      "content": "<p>Fieldwork requires patience before the frame. In this study, we break down how analytical tracking systems help map out the migratory movements of local species across the wetlands.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/uq0zgy3i/image/upload/q_auto,f_auto,w_1600/lion_pride_13_q5bwgp.jpg\" alt=\"Indian Cormorants hunting bullfrogs\">\n<span class=\"img-caption\">Figure 1: Rare documentation of hunting sequences captured at Lal Dhori.</span>\n\n<h2>The Intersection of Systems and Field Biology</h2>\n<p>By treating photography as scientific evidence rather than simple spectacle, we feed crucial dataset observations straight to environmental networks like the Bombay Natural History Society.</p>\n\n<p>Avian species exhibit nuanced behavioral patterns during twilight hours that standard observation easily misses. By combining long-duration sensor data with precision telephoto observation, our Junagadh field surveys document feeding strategies and territorial disputes in unprecedented detail.</p>",
